#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Velox: turn a short prompt into a working project.

Velox gives fast local and hosted models the tools and execution loop to take a
rough request through planning, implementation, testing and review. It keeps
long-running work moving without requiring a prompt for every next step. The
same harness handles research, writing, local files and scheduled work.

Capabilities
------------
Persistent checklists hold requirements and progress. Background agents take on
parts of a task; a separate Reviewer checks the submitted result. Native tools
cover files, Python, shell commands, terminals, web research and images. Skills,
Context Docs and optional account connections supply reusable working context.
Tool calls, model requests and results remain inspectable while a task runs.

Architecture
------------
ChatRuntime and AgentRuntime own the execution loops. LLMClient handles model
transports and context fitting; EndpointInferenceScheduler admits requests only
while they need inference capacity. ToolRegistry validates and dispatches calls.
ChecklistStore persists requirements and review state. Storage and the record
stores retain conversations and task data and validate persisted schemas.
Panels, Widgets and Renderer provide
the SDL interface. The application stays in this file; tests and their isolated
process runner live in test_velox.py.

Run python velox.py from a separate application-data directory. Use --init-only
to initialize it without opening the window. Run python test_velox.py from the
source directory for the complete regression suite. README.md covers setup;
SECURITY.md describes tool permissions and credential storage.
"""

